name: Complete Review ledger navigation and stable finding details
size: 120x36
cwd: @TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py prepare @TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 30 rows 1-500 of 1000 | first-page
nav-mode:
require-live-snap: 20 Ctrl+N | first-controls
ask: Does the first page distinguish its 500 loaded rows from the complete 1000-finding ledger and visibly offer the next page?
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | second-page
expect: Ctrl+P
submit: open F-0952
require-live-snap: 20 Synthetic Review candidate 0000 | omitted-finding-details
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 large-b | settled-details
expect: 501-1000/1000
ask: Does paging reach the previously omitted finding with its stable alias, source and decision evidence, without a separate global filter?
nav-mode:
keys: C-p
require-live-snap: 20 rows 1-500 of 1000 | back-to-first
expect: Ctrl+N
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | second-again
resize: 160x48
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | paging-160x48
expect: scope: F-0952 · Review
resize: 96x89
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | paging-96x89
resize: 80x24
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | paging-80x24
resize: 60x20
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | paging-60x20
resize: 40x12
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | paging-40x12
expect: Ctrl+P
ask: At 40x12, can the operator identify the current page and return to the previous page while retaining usable finding navigation?
keys: C-p
require-live-snap: 20 500/1000 loaded | tiny-first
expect: Ctrl+N
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | tiny-second
keys: Escape
expect-echo-within: 300 retained-paging-draft
live-snap: paging-draft
expect: retained-paging-draft
ask: Does the composer retain typing ownership and the paging draft without moving to another page?
keys: C-u
resize: 120x36
submit: findings filter name:0000
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 Synthetic Review candidate 0000 | filtered-first-page
expect: FINDINGS · 1
ask: Does changing the global query reset page position while preserving full-ledger review progress?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 30 rows 1-500 of 1000 | no-color-first
nav-mode:
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 20 501-1000/1000 | no-color-second
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py verify-read-only @TARGET @ART/fixture
ask: Does no-color restart retain complete navigation without changing observations, decisions, source bytes or spending?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
